          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q7-short-reason",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It is closer to one because ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{1}{99}<\\frac{1}{98}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{97}{98}&=1-\\frac{1}{98}\\\\\\frac{98}{99}&=1-\\frac{1}{99}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor positive unit fractions, a larger denominator gives a smaller fraction, so $\\frac{1}{99}<\\frac{1}{98}$. Thus $\\frac{98}{99}$ is closer to one and\n$$\\frac{98}{99}>\\frac{97}{98}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
